Cell["\<\
Please clone the application/leading-regge-trajectory-AdS-mass-shifts branch \
to run the notebook.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0043729635007887`*^9, 4.004373007688178*^9}, {
  4.00437306172383*^9, 4.004373068366496*^9}, {4.0044880265923157`*^9, 
  4.004488046119474*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b48e8063-8d34-4ffe-956c-\
7eee6d2170ad"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook verifies n = 1, 2 results presented in the paper \"AdS Leading \
Regge Trajectory from String Field Theory\" written by Cho, Gomide, \
Scheinpflug, and Yin. string - code generates a general form of basis of \
string fields and their string brackets, which can then be reduced to the \
ansatz used in the paper . Output of the commands in this notebook can be \
post - processed by LRTsystem . wl and Diffeosystem.wl (written with \
ClaudeCode) as shown below in the Post - processing section, which then \
verifies the linearized EOM.
Vanilla string-code takes a long time for computing level n=2,3 brackets. \
Level 2 commands compute in around 10h, level 3 takes even longer. An \
LLM-optimized run of the string-code engine was used to compute the n=3 \
results recorded in the paper.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.004528195101598*^9, 4.0045281992743797`*^9}, {
  4.004528229933267*^9, 
  4.004528337433709*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"a567922b-b72c-400c-a19d-\
58d600890b60"],

